# /review

When the user runs `/review`, follow these steps:

1. Determine which file to read:
   - If the user specifies a filename (e.g. `/review proposals.generated.md`), use that file.
   - Otherwise default to `proposals.md`.
2. Read the file from the project root.
3. Parse every `## ` heading as a proposal title. Collect the body text below each heading as the proposal body (everything up to the next `## ` or end of file).
4. Follow the instructions in `.cursor/prompts/review.md` exactly.
5. Write the resulting `session.json` to the project root.
6. Tell the user to run this command to clear the app and reload from the new session.json:
   ```bash
   curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/reset
   ```
7. Confirm to the user: which file was read, how many proposals were loaded, and what `session.json` now contains.

Only trigger this rule when the user message starts with `/review` or explicitly asks to load proposals into the app.
